**Goal** — Wire all new check phases and fix strategies into `buildPlanForStrategy`, extend `StoryOrchestratorResult` with `rectificationExhausted`/`unfixedFindings`, and extend `applyPostRunInspection` with the `mechanicalFailedOnly` rule and D3 ctx field derivations.

**Motivation** — US-003 and US-004 added the building blocks; this story activates them in the execution path so the unified builder handles lint, typecheck, scoped-verify, and rectification end-to-end.

**Approach**

**1. PlanInputs slot population** — Add new optional slots to `PlanInputs` and populate them in `assemblePlanInputsFromCtx` subject to config gating:

```typescript
// src/execution/plan-inputs.ts (post-migration shape — new optional fields)
export interface PlanInputs {
  // ... existing fields unchanged ...
  readonly verifyScoped?: VerifyScopedInput;      // new: non-TDD only
  readonly lintCheck?: LintCheckInput;             // new: gated by review.checks ∋ "lint" && lint command configured
  readonly typecheckCheck?: TypecheckCheckInput;   // new: gated by review.checks ∋ "typecheck" && typecheck command configured
  // semanticReview / adversarialReview gating: inlineReviewEnabled condition removed here (last gating-site)
}
```

The `inlineReviewEnabled` condition is removed from ALL remaining slot-population sites in `assemblePlanInputsFromCtx` — including `semanticReviewInput` and `adversarialReviewInput`. After this story, `inlineReview` flag has zero remaining gates (AC-005a.2).

**2. buildPlanForStrategy wiring** — Add new check phases and strategy assembly:

```typescript
// src/execution/build-plan-for-strategy.ts (post-migration excerpt)
// Non-TDD: add verify-scoped
if (!isThreeSession && inputs.verifyScoped) builder.addVerifyScoped(inputs.verifyScoped);

// Check phases (gated by slot presence)
if (inputs.lintCheck) builder.addLintCheck(inputs.lintCheck);
if (inputs.typecheckCheck) builder.addTypecheckCheck(inputs.typecheckCheck);

// Strategy assembly (priority encoded by array position; each entry conditional)
const strategies: FixStrategy<Finding, any, any, any>[] = [];
if (config.quality.commands.lintFix || config.quality.commands.lintFixScoped) {
  strategies.push(makeMechanicalLintFixStrategy());
}
if (config.quality.commands.formatFix || config.quality.commands.formatFixScoped) {
  strategies.push(makeMechanicalFormatFixStrategy());
}
if (isThreeSession && inputs.fullSuiteGate) {
  strategies.push(makeFullSuiteRectifyStrategy(story));
}
if (config.quality.autofix?.enabled !== false) {
  strategies.push(makeAutofixImplementerStrategy(ctx));
  strategies.push(makeAutofixTestWriterStrategy(ctx));
}
```

**3. StoryOrchestratorResult extension:**

```typescript
// src/execution/story-orchestrator.ts (post-migration shape)
export interface StoryOrchestratorResult {
  readonly success: boolean;
  readonly phaseCosts: Record<string, number>;
  readonly totalCostUsd: number;
  readonly durationMs: number;
  readonly phaseOutputs: Record<string, unknown>;
  /** Set by runRectification when inner FixCycle exits via max-attempts or bail-when with remaining findings. */
  readonly rectificationExhausted?: boolean;
  /** Findings remaining when cycle exited. Set together with rectificationExhausted. */
  readonly unfixedFindings?: readonly Finding[];
}
```

`runRectification` writes both fields when `cycleResult.exitReason !== "no-findings-applicable"` and `cycleResult.finalFindings.length > 0`.

**4. applyPostRunInspection extensions:**

A) `mechanicalFailedOnly` rule ported from `autofix.ts:182-199`:
```typescript
// src/execution/post-run.ts (excerpt)
if (planResult.rectificationExhausted &&
    planResult.unfixedFindings &&
    planResult.unfixedFindings.length > 0) {
  const sources = new Set(planResult.unfixedFindings.map(f => f.source));
  const allMechanical = [...sources].every(s => s === "lint" || s === "typecheck");
  if (allMechanical) {
    logger.warn("execution", "Mechanical-only failure unfixable — proceeding (LLM review passed)",
      { storyId: ctx.story.id });
    return { /* continue, no escalation */ };
  }
}
```

B) D3 ctx field derivations — three new ctx fields from `planResult.phaseOutputs`:
- `ctx.verifyPassed: boolean` — derived from `phaseOutputs["verifier"]` (TDD) or `phaseOutputs["verify-scoped"]` (non-TDD)
- `ctx.semanticReviewResult: { passed, findings } | undefined` — from `phaseOutputs["semantic-review"]`, undefined when absent
- `ctx.rectificationIterationCount: number` — from rectification phase's iteration count, `0` when absent

Legacy fields `ctx.reviewResult` / `ctx.verifyResult` / `ctx.autofixAttempt` remain populated by their existing stages this story; deletion is US-005c.

**Do not yet delete legacy stages or the `inlineReview` schema field** — that is US-005c.

**Scope**
In:
- `src/execution/plan-inputs.ts` — new slots, remove last `inlineReviewEnabled` gates
- `src/execution/build-plan-for-strategy.ts` — wire check phases and strategies
- `src/execution/story-orchestrator.ts` — extend `StoryOrchestratorResult`, update `runRectification`
- `src/execution/post-run.ts` — `mechanicalFailedOnly` rule + D3 ctx field derivations

Out:
- Legacy pipeline stages NOT deleted (US-005c)
- `inlineReview` schema field NOT deleted from `schemas-execution.ts` (US-005c)
